 by AIPAC. And (spoiler) he does a pretty good job.\n\nWorth listening to:\nhttps://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5903129/tucker-carlson-trump-iran-war-interview", "author": "SuperDuperBasedMD", "created": 1790490866655, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "sub-collector", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Tucker on NPR", "last_comment_created": 1790499339831, "content": "<p>NPR is propaganda. Their goal is to split MAGA. Duh.</p>\n<p>Tucker, knows he's being used, knows that this hurts MAGA and hurts the US but he thinks that all these effects were baked into the cake once we decided to go to war with Iran. His goal is to make the best of a bad situation and use this opportunity to throw off the yoke of AIPAC. His anti-Trump criticism is bait to get normies to listen as he points out government capture by AIPAC. And (spoiler) he does a pretty good job.</p>\n<p>Worth listening to:\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5903129/tucker-carlson-trump-iran-war-interview\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5903129/tucker-carlson-trump-iran-war-interview</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 10, "is_edited": true, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVQvo88b", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 23, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8857805, "raw_content": "", "author": "ashl